{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "log-08-linked-exponential-relations",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Linked Exponential and Variable-Base Relations",
    "description": "Turn linked power relations into logarithms and simplify variable-base expressions without solving more than necessary.",
    "teachingApproach": "Use relationships between bases as algebraic structure, not as invitations to calculate every variable. Derive one relation at a time, show the cancellation, and use fresh values to test the same pattern.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 10, Logarithms. Teach variable-base relations drawn from the chapter: log_a(ab)=x and the linked value log_b(ab), inverse-base/inverse-argument pairs, a=b^x, b=c^y, c=a^z giving xyz=1, and a=b^2=c^3=d^4. Convert equal powers a^x=b^y to x log a=y log b, and use chained exponent equations where intermediate logarithms cancel. Finish with paired equations such as 3^(x−y)=27 and 3^(x+y)=243. Emphasize reshaping the given relation before solving individual variables."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's work with logarithms where the bases themselves are linked.\n\nThese questions often look complicated because several letters appear, but the goal is usually to reshape the relation until something cancels.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose log_a(ab)=x.\n\nSplit the product:\nlog_a a + log_a b = x\n1 + log_a b = x.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So log_a b=x−1.\n\nThis small relation is the bridge to any log involving a and b.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "If log₂(2b)=5, what is b?",
